DISPUTE CORRESPONDENCE - CONTRACTOR'S LETTERS

Letter No. PG/2024/089
Date: 01.07.2024

To:
The Managing Director,
RVPNL, Jaipur

Subject: Right of Way (RoW) Not Handed Over - Transmission Line
Reference: Work Order No. RVPNL/2024-25/220kV/2890

Dear Sir,

We refer to the site possession given on 25.05.2024. However, we observe that the Right of Way
for the 45 km 220 kV transmission line has not been handed over due to land acquisition issues.

This is causing complete obstruction to transmission line construction from Tower No. 15 to
Tower No. 45. We request RVPNL to expedite land acquisition to avoid project delays.

Per RVPNL GCC Clause 6 (Site Possession), this delay shall be considered as Employer's delay
and shall be compensable.

Yours faithfully,
For M/s. Power Grid Infra Projects Pvt. Ltd.
Project Manager

***

Letter No. PG/2024/145
Date: 01.11.2024

To:
The Managing Director,
RVPNL, Jaipur

Subject: Extension of Time Request - RoW and Equipment Delays
Reference: Our Letter No. PG/2024/089 dated 01.07.2024

Dear Sir,

We submit this formal request for Extension of Time (EOT) under RVPNL GCC Clause 44:

EOT Request 1: Transmission Line RoW Delay
- Delay period: 120 days (01.07.2024 to 28.10.2024)
- Reason: Land acquisition issues beyond contractor's control
- Impact: Transmission line construction completely stopped

EOT Request 2: 220 kV GIS Equipment Supply Delay
- Expected delay: 240 days (RVPNL to supply equipment within 6 months of site handover)
- Current status: Equipment not yet supplied by RVPNL
- Impact: Substation civil works cannot be completed without GIS equipment

Total EOT requested: 360 days

Yours faithfully,
For M/s. Power Grid Infra Projects Pvt. Ltd.
Director

***

Letter No. PG/2025/189
Date: 01.02.2025

To:
The Managing Director,
RVPNL, Jaipur

Subject: Notice of Equipment Supply Delay - 220 kV GIS Equipment
Reference: Work Order No. RVPNL/2024-25/220kV/2890

Dear Sir,

We refer to Clause 15 of the Contract which stipulates that RVPNL shall supply the 220 kV GIS
equipment within 6 months of site handover (i.e., by 25.11.2024).

As of 01.02.2025, the GIS equipment has not been supplied. This delay of 68 days is causing:
- Tower crane and heavy machinery idle at substation site
- 45 specialized electrical workers idle
- Civil works cannot be completed without equipment dimensions
- Testing and commissioning schedule completely disrupted

We request RVPNL to immediately supply the GIS equipment or compensate for the delay
as per RVPNL GCC Clause 10CA (Price Escalation) and Clause 44 (Employer's Delay).

Yours faithfully,
For M/s. Power Grid Infra Projects Pvt. Ltd.
Director